 - Only managers may delete tasks.
 - Archived projects reject all writes with 409 (reads still work).
 - A task ID that does not belong to the project in the path → 404.
+- Moving a task (`POST .../move`) takes it from the project in the path to
+  `toProjectId`. Its ID, title, status and assignee are kept.
+  - The caller must be a manager of the source project (else 403; archived → 409),
+    because the task leaves that project, as with delete.
+  - The destination must be readable by the caller (missing, in another
+    organization, or not readable → 404). The caller must be a contributor or
+    manager there (else 403; archived → 409).
+  - Moving to the project the task is already in → 400.
+  - The assignee must be a contributor or manager of the destination, since
+    the assignee is kept. Otherwise → 400 and nothing changes.
 
